                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Norman OK",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 14 at 10:32AM CDT until October 14 at 12:45PM CDT by NWS Norman OK",
                "description": "FFWOUN\n\nThe National Weather Service in Norman has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorthwestern Cleveland County in central Oklahoma...\nNorthern Grady County in central Oklahoma...\nNorthwestern McClain County in central Oklahoma...\n\n* Until 1245 PM CDT.\n\n* At 1032 AM CDT, broadcast media reported widespread flash flooding\nfrom thunderstorms in the area. Between 2 and 5 inches of rain have\nfallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are possible\nin the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Broadcast media reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSouthwestern Oklahoma City, Norman, Moore, Chickasha, Newcastle,\nBlanchard, Tuttle, Goldsby, Union City, Minco, Verden, Amber,\nBridge Creek, Pocasset, Norge, Middleberg, Tabler, Stanley Draper\nLake, southwestern Lake Thunderbird and Ninnekah.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
