                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 14 at 10:17AM CDT until October 14 at 12:30PM CDT by NWS Norman OK",
                "description": "FFWOUN\n\nThe National Weather Service in Norman has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorthwestern Greer County in southwestern Oklahoma...\nNorthern Harmon County in southwestern Oklahoma...\nNorthern Kiowa County in southwestern Oklahoma...\nBeckham County in western Oklahoma...\nCuster County in western Oklahoma...\nSouthern Roger Mills County in western Oklahoma...\nWashita County in western Oklahoma...\n\n* Until 1230 PM CDT.\n\n* At 1017 AM CDT, the public reported thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain in Elk City, Clinton, Custer City, Cordell. Between 3 and 10\ninches of rain have fallen. Little to no rainfall is expected in\nthe next several hours, but more rain is likely this afternoon and\ntonight. Flash flooding impacts will continue.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Public reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nElk City, Weatherford, Clinton, Sayre, Cordell, Burns Flat, Thomas,\nErick, Sentinel, Arapaho, Mountain View, Hammon, Dill City, Canute,\nCorn, Custer City, Butler, Carter, Bessie and Rocky.",
