                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 14 at 8:34AM CDT until October 14 at 11:30AM CDT by NWS Norman OK",
                "description": "FFWOUN\n\nThe National Weather Service in Norman has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorthern Canadian County in central Oklahoma...\nSouthern Kingfisher County in central Oklahoma...\nSouthern Blaine County in northwestern Oklahoma...\nNorthwestern Caddo County in southwestern Oklahoma...\nSoutheastern Custer County in western Oklahoma...\nNortheastern Washita County in western Oklahoma...\n\n* Until 1130 AM CDT.\n\n* At 834 AM CDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain in Weatherford, Hydro,\nBridgeport, Hinton, Geary, Okarche, and Kingfisher. Between 5 and 9\ninches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 2 to 4\ninches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing\nor expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nEl Reno, Weatherford, Watonga, Kingfisher, Piedmont, Hinton, Geary,\nOkarche, Hydro, Calumet, Corn, Eakly, Lookeba, Colony, Bridgeport,\nGreenfield, Concho, Cedar Lake and Omega.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
